{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"91276961524ae057cebe385f39f3660e82a58588efad6d3169fdb0baafb69747","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_beaebf7b0e78e33c63ed4639209c272bfe7764fb841147a25208112e9785b8ad","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically sound and well-motivated approach to semi-supervised learning. The methodological design is consistent, and the experimental evaluation is robust, featuring multiple runs and clear comparisons against relevant baselines. The authors provide sufficient architectural details for reproduction, though specific hyperparameters are deferred to an appendix not included in the provided text.","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_identity_sha256":"b3f251d2d23507343c1f476c21f5137d794144b95be23761e9ee0a4272ef53e0","prompt_identity_sha256":"bfac759dd8aaa8b6ae9d6b6aa53e78f9b38a47e187ebb7211d2638354a42cdf7","raw_response_sha256":"8d51826407904178cac4bf46aa5baab45b2f4567facc219ea71486c6ecf21017","request_identity_sha256":"d317469a73220d4bbdcb55018ac563fd20a6acbd3ee6c18d0b3f2d7fd4812362","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"4665a6a172d64a89dedcf8e3ec21323ba91ff11a831e10731f470cd8c9c78a9d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-007","SRC-011"],"review_text":"The proposed methods, the Pi-model and temporal ensembling, are mathematically well-formulated. The Pi-model correctly utilizes the stochastic nature of dropout to create a consistency loss between two evaluations of the same input. The temporal ensembling method introduces a momentum-based accumulation of predictions with a bias correction term, which is a standard and appropriate technique for handling the initialization of moving averages. The loss functions are clearly defined, and the algorithms are presented with sufficient pseudocode to verify their logical structure.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The experimental design is adequate for the claims made. The authors evaluate their methods on two standard benchmarks, CIFAR-10 and SVHN, using multiple label budgets (500, 1000, 4000, and all labels). The inclusion of both augmented and non-augmented results allows for a fair comparison with prior work that may not have used data augmentation. The results are reported as means and standard deviations over 10 runs, which provides a reasonable basis for assessing the stability of the improvements. The comparison against state-of-the-art methods like the GAN of Salimans et al. and the Gamma-model is appropriate for the 2017 context.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-009","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The paper provides a detailed table describing the network architecture, including layer types, filter sizes, and activation functions. However, the specific training hyperparameters, such as the learning rate, batch size, and the exact form of the ramp-up function w(t), are stated to be in Appendix A, which is not included in the provided text. While the architecture is clear, the absence of these specific training details in the main body limits the immediate reproducibility of the results without access to the full appendix or code.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The paper compares its methods against several relevant prior works, including the Gamma-model, CatGAN, and various GAN-based semi-supervised learning approaches. The related work section provides a clear positioning of the proposed methods relative to ladder networks and bootstrapping techniques. The comparisons are fair, as the authors explicitly note the use or non-use of data augmentation to ensure comparability with baselines that may have used different preprocessing pipelines.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017"],"review_text":"The statistical rigor is supported by the reporting of mean and standard deviation over 10 independent runs for the main results. This allows for an assessment of the variance in the model's performance. The standard deviations are generally small for the proposed methods, suggesting stable training. While no formal significance tests are reported, the magnitude of the improvements relative to the reported standard deviations suggests that the results are statistically meaningful.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"46e90b2d9f8b6f1592ad9def3e06a229116d649e7bc319286a117d6eec53b29e","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","paper_ordinal":21,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"8d51826407904178cac4bf46aa5baab45b2f4567facc219ea71486c6ecf21017","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ6oOfqge","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"cff505150bd9863867e71b62a1d31f203b54555a214198a8e9035f710c340b4f","request_identity_sha256":"d317469a73220d4bbdcb55018ac563fd20a6acbd3ee6c18d0b3f2d7fd4812362","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":927,"prompt_tokens":15256,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":16183},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"d317469a73220d4bbdcb55018ac563fd20a6acbd3ee6c18d0b3f2d7fd4812362","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}